#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: grapes 40
#> pause: 40
#> must: , 1 apples 12, 2 bananas 30, 4 dates 16, 6 grapes 40
#> not: cherries
#> not: figs
#> source: $!d
# 5. H collects, x gets it back. Sheet: "H" appends to the hold buffer with a "\n" between.
# Every line with an a is appended to the hold buffer; $!d throws all but the last
# line away. On the last line x brings the collection into the pattern space and
# the s///g turns each newline into ", ". The leading ", " is real: the hold buffer
# was empty before the first H, and H still put a newline in front of apples.
# Try: change the first line to "1h" and add "1!H": h overwrites instead of appending.
/a/H
$!d
x
s/\n/, /g

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
